like {lo ka ce'u ce'u bramau} etc. (The word "comparison" is present in=20
the English definition of {porsi}).

Provided that porsi2 is an unary property of porsi1, the below is a=20
possible way to define the sequence [b,r,o,d,a] using {porsi}:

=E2=80=A2 { porsi  fa B ce'o R ce'o O ce'o D ce'o O  fi B ce R ce O ce D  f=
e=20
loka ce'u poi'i ge ke'a pormei li mu gi fi ke'a li'erla'i fa B fe R gi'e=20
li'erla'i fa R fe O gi'e li'erla'i fa O fe D gi'e li'erla'i fa D fe O }

And building an ordered set from the set {A, B, C} by sorting them by=20
size would require putting something like the below into porsi2:

=E2=80=A2 { lo ka ro da ro de zo'u ganai da de ce'u lidne gi da de branalme=
'a }

However then the place structure of {porsi} seems a little awkward, as=20
porsi3 is not necessary anymore and claiming "porsi1 cu ckaji fe porsi2"=20
is enough.

